      "text": "To determine how far Jana will walk in 10 minutes, we start by considering her walking rate. We know that it takes her 24 minutes to walk one mile. Therefore, we can calculate her walking speed or rate of 1 mile per 24 minutes. We need to find out how far she will walk in 10 minutes.\n\nTo do this, we can set up a proportion based on her speed. The proportion can be written as:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{24 \\text{ minutes}}{1 \\text{ mile}} = \\frac{10 \\text{ minutes}}{x \\text{ miles}}\n\\]\n\nHere \\( x \\) is the distance Jana walks in 10 minutes. To solve for \\( x \\), we can cross multiply and then solve for \\( x \\):\n\n\\[\n24x = 10\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{10}{24}\n\\]\n\nNext, to convert \\( x \\) to a decimal, we perform the division:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{24} = 0.4\n\\]\n\nTherefore, if Jana walks in 24 minutes for 1 mile, she walks \\( 0.4 \\) miles in 10 minutes. Thus, the answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.4}\n\\]",
