      "text": "To determine how far Jana will walk in 10 minutes, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate Jana's walking rate in miles per minute.\n2. Use this rate to find out how far she walks in 10 minutes.\n\n### Step 1: Calculate Jana's rate\n\nJana takes 24 minutes to walk 1 mile. Therefore, her walking rate is:\n\\[\n\\text{Rate} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}}\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Use the rate to find distance\n\nWe need to find out how far Jana can walk in 10 minutes. Using the rate we calculated:\n\\[\n\\text{Distance in 10 minutes} = \\text{Rate} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nPlugging in the rate:\n\\[\n\\text{Distance in 10 minutes} = \\frac{1 \\text{ mile}}{24 \\text{ minutes}} \\times 10 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Simplify the calculation\n\n\\[\n\\text{Distance in 10 minutes} = \\frac{10}{24} \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\nNow, simplify \\(\\frac{10}{24}\\).\n\n### Step 4: Calculate the numerical value\n\nTo convert \\(\\frac{10}{24}\\) into a decimal, divide 10 by 24:\n\\[\n\\frac{10}{24} = 0.416666\\ldots \\approx 0.417 \\text{ miles}\n\\]\n\n### Step 5: Round the result to the nearest tenth\n\nWhen rounding 0.417 to the nearest tenth, the digit in the tenths place (4) remains unchanged and we look at the hundredths place (1). Since the hundredths place is less than 5, we do not round up.\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0.4 \\text{ miles}}\n\\]",
